@startuml
title Abstract Factory / Kit

skinparam legendBackgroundColor #f9f9f9
skinparam legendBorderColor #999999

legend right

**Intent**:
Create families of related/dependent objects without specifying concrete classes.

**Motivation**:
You need to ensure products are created from the same family and can vary together
(e.g., GUI themes, database drivers).

**Applicability**:
You need products from the same “family” to be used together.
Need to vary the family at runtime/configuration time.
Enforce compatibility constraints among created objects.

**Participants & Collaborations**:
AbstractFactory defines creation methods per product type.
ConcreteFactoryX produces matching concrete products.
Client uses the factory and remains agnostic to concretes.

**Consequences**:
Pros: Ensures product consistency; isolates concrete classes; supports switching families.
Cons: More classes/interfaces; rigid when adding new product types (requires updating all factories).

**Implementation Notes**:
Use composition/dependency injection to pass chosen factory into clients.
Consider factories as singletons or configured via a container.
Often paired with Factory Method inside concrete factories.

**Known Uses**:
Java javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilderFactory, javax.net.ssl.SSLContext
GUI factories in Swing/JavaFX; DI containers assembling families of services.

**Related Patterns**:
Factory Method, Builder, Prototype; often combined with Facade and DI/Configuration.

endlegend

interface AbstractProductA
interface AbstractProductB

interface AbstractFactory {
  +createA() : AbstractProductA
  +createB() : AbstractProductB
}

class ConcreteFactory1
class ConcreteFactory2

class ConcreteProductA1
class ConcreteProductB1
class ConcreteProductA2
class ConcreteProductB2

AbstractFactory <|.. ConcreteFactory1
AbstractFactory <|.. ConcreteFactory2

AbstractProductA <|.. ConcreteProductA1
AbstractProductA <|.. ConcreteProductA2
AbstractProductB <|.. ConcreteProductB1
AbstractProductB <|.. ConcreteProductB2

ConcreteFactory1 ..> ConcreteProductA1 : creates
ConcreteFactory1 ..> ConcreteProductB1 : creates
ConcreteFactory2 ..> ConcreteProductA2 : creates
ConcreteFactory2 ..> ConcreteProductB2 : creates

class Client
Client ..> AbstractFactory : uses
Client ..> AbstractProductA
Client ..> AbstractProductB
@enduml